  "content": "Imported flowers to be restricted in KMC during Tihar festival\nRastriya Samachar Samiti (RSS)\nFriday, October 10, 2025\n0\nComments\nKathmandu, October 10\nThe Kathmandu Metropolitan City has announced a ban on the supply of imported flowers and flower products within the city during the upcoming Tihar festival.\nAt a press meet held today, the Metropolitan Police Force stated that the decision aims to promote domestic farmers. Similarly, the local government will establish flower supply centers at 32 locations, including NB Centre in New Baneshwor, Phoenix Tower in Shankhamul, Sifal Chaur, Chabahil Ganeshthan, KL Tower, Old Baneshwor, and Star Mall in Putalisadak, from October 17 to 22.\nThe Force also announced plans to confiscate flowers if they are found to be imported. At the event, President of Floriculture Association of Nepal, Rajesh Bhakta Shrestha, expressed support for the local government’s policy. He also shared that the Association will be organizing the 18th Godavari (Chrysanthemum) Flower Competition from October 15 to 18.\nAccording to the Association, domestic flower production is sufficient to meet market demand.\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\nBP Highway\nFlowers\nnational women team\nRastriya Samachar Samiti (RSS)\nRSS is a government-run national news portal of Nepal.\nMore From the Author\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nJacaranda in Kathmandu: A beautiful flower’s ‘invasive’ love affair with Nepal’s capital\n2 years ago\nNepal self-sufficient in flowers this Tihar\n5 years ago\nMost Read\nHighways blocked nationwide as heavy rainfall disrupts travel\nUAE introduces new rules for Visit Visa Sponsorship\nFlood risks in Kathmandu, KMC launches helpline service\nGold price surges by Rs 10,000 per tola after Dashain\nGold price reaches record high at Rs 235,960 per tola\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nCharred body found at Koteshwor Bhatbhateni, Gen-Z protest death toll rises to 74\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nNo consensus on Hami Nepal’s claim of leading the Gen-Z movement\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nDecades-old irrigation projects stall as Madhesh faces drought, food crisis looms\n3 months ago\nEditor's Pick\nNepal’s farming crisis: When plans stay on paper and fields suffer\n3 months ago\nAlso Read\nPolitics\nWho do student unions stand for? Questions rise after Gen Z Movement\n14 hours ago\nEconomy\nThai AirAsia to resume flights from Gautam Buddha International Airport\n14 hours ago\nFestival\nFlowers ready for Tihar Festival (Photos)\n14 hours ago\nOpinion\nGen Z movement in Nepal at a crossroads: Between reform, revolt and reflection\n2 days ago\nSociety\nDiversions built at 3 sections of BP Highway\n2 days ago",
